[ Laughter ]

00:00:52.652 --> 00:00:54.988 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Please welcome to the sho
Dave Grohl.

00:00:54.988 --> 00:00:56.723 line:92%
It's so nice to see you, Dave.

00:00:56.723 --> 00:00:59.125 align:start size:94% position:6%
-How you doing, Seth?
-I'm doing great.

00:00:59.125 --> 00:01:01.628
This is really wonderful,
this docuseries, 'cause

00:01:01.628 --> 00:01:04.497 size:84% position:42%
this is based on a book
that your mom wrote.

00:01:04.497 --> 00:01:07.967 align:start size:94% position:6%
She went out and interviewed
other musician's moms.

00:01:07.967 --> 00:01:11.104 align:start size:94% position:6%
Was this an idea
she had on her own?

00:01:11.104 --> 00:01:11.805 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-Yeah, it was, actually.

00:01:11.805 --> 00:01:14.441
So, my mother was a public
schoolteacher for 35 years

00:01:14.441 --> 00:01:18.978 align:start size:94% position:6%
and when she retired, you know
I told her -- I'm like,

00:01:18.978 --> 00:01:22.215
"Don't do that cruise-ship thing
that all retirees do."

00:01:22.215 --> 00:01:24.017 size:78% position:39%
I was like -- just --
I have a cruise ship.

00:01:24.017 --> 00:01:26.186 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was like, "Jump on
the tour bus. Let's go."

00:01:26.186 --> 00:01:27.353 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so I took her
around the world.

00:01:27.353 --> 00:01:30.723 align:start size:94% position:6%
I took her to Australia
and Japan and all over Europe.

00:01:30.723 --> 00:01:33.393 align:start size:94% position:6%
And in our travels,
she was like,

00:01:33.393 --> 00:01:35.228 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Where are all
the other mothers?

00:01:35.228 --> 00:01:38.665 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, how come
other moms don't hang out

00:01:38.665 --> 00:01:40.400 line:92%
at their kids' rock shows, too?"

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:43.103
Which she always had.
I mean, she was the coolest mom.

00:01:43.103 --> 00:01:44.838 align:start size:94% position:6%
Growing up,
she took me to jazz clubs,

00:01:44.838 --> 00:01:47.574 align:start size:94% position:6%
and she always came
to punk-rock shows.

00:01:47.574 --> 00:01:50.777 align:start size:94% position:6%
So she decided to go hunt down
all the other mothers,

00:01:50.777 --> 00:01:53.379 align:start size:94% position:6%
and she made calls
to Dr. Dre's mother

00:01:53.379 --> 00:01:55.915
and Pharrell's mother,
Miranda Lambert's mother,

00:01:55.915 --> 00:01:58.451
and Geddy Lee's mother,
all these different moms,

00:01:58.451 --> 00:02:01.054 size:88% position:44%
and she interviewed them
and wrote a book called

00:02:01.054 --> 00:02:02.689 align:start size:94% position:6%
"From Cradle to Stage,"
and in that book,

00:02:02.689 --> 00:02:07.727
she realized that there were
these really clear parallels

00:02:07.727 --> 00:02:08.962 line:92%
in all of the relationship

00:02:08.962 --> 00:02:10.830 align:start size:94% position:6%
between the mother
and the artist.

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:12.832 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then, after the book,
we were like,

00:02:12.832 --> 00:02:15.335
"Well, let's turn it into
a documentary series."

00:02:15.335 --> 00:02:17.337 line:92%
-I mean, the mothers who -

00:02:17.337 --> 00:02:19.038 align:start size:94% position:6%
the mothers of rock stars
or any musicians,

00:02:19.038 --> 00:02:21.574 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's truly amazing
how supportive they have to be

00:02:21.574 --> 00:02:23.176 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because even
if they loved music,

00:02:23.176 --> 00:02:25.011 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's very likely
that their children

00:02:25.011 --> 00:02:26.012 line:92%
will make a kind of music

00:02:26.012 --> 00:02:30.049 align:start size:94% position:6%
that is not the same
as what they loved growing up.

00:02:30.049 --> 00:02:32.685 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-But you said your mom

00:02:32.685 --> 00:02:34.154 line:92%
came to early shows of yours

00:02:34.154 --> 00:02:36.589
when it was maybe not --
-Oh, yeah. She was always there.

00:02:36.589 --> 00:02:41.094 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, she, like --
You know, I think that --

00:02:41.094 --> 00:02:46.633 align:start size:94% position:6%
that, as a parent,
you have to understand

00:02:46.633 --> 00:02:48.301 line:92%
and accept and appreciate

00:02:48.301 --> 00:02:51.337 align:start size:94% position:6%
your child becoming
an individual, right?

00:02:51.337 --> 00:02:55.241 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so, with musicians,
they usually decide

00:02:55.241 --> 00:02:58.077 align:start size:94% position:6%
in between the ages
of, like, 11 and 13

00:02:58.077 --> 00:03:00.980 size:81% position:41%
that that's going to
become their identity.

00:03:00.980 --> 00:03:03.016 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know. "I'm a musician.
You know?

00:03:03.016 --> 00:03:07.320 size:88% position:44%
So it's a parent's job
to, like, show them love

00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:08.721 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then just
get out of the way.

00:03:08.721 --> 00:03:12.225 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because that's
what their heart --

00:03:12.225 --> 00:03:13.660 align:start size:94% position:6%
that's what their heart
lives for.

00:03:13.660 --> 00:03:15.528 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so that's -- I'm sure --
You know,

00:03:15.528 --> 00:03:17.897 size:84% position:42%
my mom wasn't listening
to the Dead Kennedys

00:03:17.897 --> 00:03:20.700 align:start size:94% position:6%
and Slayer with me every day
you know?

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:23.336 align:start size:94% position:6%
But she did appreciate
that, you know,

00:03:23.336 --> 00:03:24.470 line:92%
I was becoming my own person

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:28.208 align:start size:94% position:6%
And fortunately, she gave me
the freedom to do that.

00:03:28.208 --> 00:03:30.009 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You -- You are someone
who strikes me

00:03:30.009 --> 00:03:32.278 align:start size:94% position:6%
as the kind of person
who says yes

00:03:32.278 --> 00:03:34.247 align:start size:94% position:6%
whenever an opportunity
presents itself.

00:03:34.247 --> 00:03:37.217
One of the things you've
said yes to over the years

00:03:37.217 --> 00:03:39.319 align:start size:94% position:6%
is being a musical guest
at "SNL"

00:03:39.319 --> 00:03:43.656 align:start size:94% position:6%
sometimes with
very, very short notice.

00:03:43.656 --> 00:03:45.592 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
Well, I mean -- So I --

00:03:45.592 --> 00:03:47.660 align:start size:94% position:6%
One of the great luxuries
of my life

00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:52.565 align:start size:94% position:6%
is that I've had the honor
to play that show --

00:03:52.565 --> 00:03:54.834 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's like 14 times
or something now.

00:03:54.834 --> 00:03:57.837 line:92%
And so -- But starting in 1992

00:03:57.837 --> 00:04:00.173 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I got to see
all of these amazing casts

00:04:00.173 --> 00:04:02.375 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, I'm not sure
when I met you,

00:04:02.375 --> 00:04:05.044 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I'm sure
it was 15 years ago.

00:04:05.044 --> 00:04:06.980 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know?
-Yeah.

00:04:06.980 --> 00:04:11.284
-So -- So being able, like
to be a part of the show

00:04:11.284 --> 00:04:14.454 align:start size:94% position:6%
is something huge,
and the process is usually..

00:04:14.454 --> 00:04:17.056 align:start size:94% position:6%
your manager
calls the publicist,

00:04:17.056 --> 00:04:19.792 align:start size:94% position:6%
calls the show,
calls the record company,

00:04:19.792 --> 00:04:22.662 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it's months and months
of preparation.

00:04:22.662 --> 00:04:24.831 align:start size:94% position:6%
The last time
the Foo Fighters played,

00:04:24.831 --> 00:04:27.634 align:start size:94% position:6%
Lorne called on Tuesday
and said,

00:04:27.634 --> 00:04:29.902
"Hey, do you want to play
'Saturday Night Live'?"

00:04:29.902 --> 00:04:31.804 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we said,
"Of course! When?"

00:04:31.804 --> 00:04:32.538 size:88% position:44% line:92%
And he said, "Saturday."

00:04:32.538 --> 00:04:36.609
And so we literally, like,
loaded our guitars onto a plane,

00:04:36.609 --> 00:04:38.645 line:92%
flew out as fast as we could

00:04:38.645 --> 00:04:40.580 line:92%
Dave Chappelle was the host.

00:04:40.580 --> 00:04:43.283 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it was great
to be back again.

00:04:43.283 --> 00:04:46.519 align:start size:94% position:6%
But what made it really specia
was that Saturday,

00:04:46.519 --> 00:04:50.857 align:start size:94% position:6%
that morning was the day
that they called the election,

00:04:50.857 --> 00:04:54.494 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
and that -- that --

00:04:54.494 --> 00:04:56.696 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
the -- the news

00:04:56.696 --> 00:04:58.931 align:start size:94% position:6%
said that Biden
was the president.

00:04:58.931 --> 00:05:03.202 align:start size:94% position:6%
So the -- the energy
in the studio was crazy.

00:05:03.202 --> 00:05:06.072 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You did it once
with Mick Jagger.

00:05:06.072 --> 00:05:06.973 size:84% position:42% line:92%
You were the musical --

00:05:06.973 --> 00:05:08.508 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm sorry. You weren't
the musical guest.

00:05:08.508 --> 00:05:10.510 align:start size:94% position:6%
You were Mick Jagger's band.
-Yeah.

00:05:10.510 --> 00:05:13.479 align:start size:94% position:6%
That was funny
because that day I was --

00:05:13.479 --> 00:05:18.117
I was literally sitting
on the toilet when Lorne called.

00:05:18.117 --> 00:05:19.986 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I answered the phone
and I said, "Hello?"

00:05:19.986 --> 00:05:21.854 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's like,
"Hold for Lorne Michaels."

00:05:21.854 --> 00:05:22.588 size:84% position:42% line:92%
I'm like, "Oh, my God."

00:05:22.588 --> 00:05:25.391
And he's like, "Uh, David, uh,
just wanted to call and say --

00:05:25.391 --> 00:05:29.028
He was saying that Mick
was going to be the host,

00:05:29.028 --> 00:05:30.129 line:92%
but he didn't have a band.

00:05:30.129 --> 00:05:32.799 size:88% position:44%
So he called and asked
if we would be his band.

00:05:32.799 --> 00:05:34.767 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, you know,
of course we said --

00:05:34.767 --> 00:05:38.071 align:start size:94% position:6%
I said, "Of course."
Like, we're going to be there.

00:05:38.071 --> 00:05:39.572 line:92%
And I looked at my schedule,

00:05:39.572 --> 00:05:42.141 align:start size:94% position:6%
realized that we had a sho
that night.

00:05:42.141 --> 00:05:43.576 line:92%
I think it was in New Jersey

00:05:43.576 --> 00:05:47.480 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so I said, "Okay.
I'll make that show go away.

00:05:47.480 --> 00:05:49.649 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because there was no way
I was missing this opportunity

00:05:49.649 --> 00:05:51.050 size:75% position:38%
I called my manager.
He says, "You can't

00:05:51.050 --> 00:05:53.252 size:84% position:42%
make that show go away.
It's already sold out.

00:05:53.252 --> 00:05:54.420 size:81% position:41% line:92%
You're the headliner."

00:05:54.420 --> 00:05:58.257 align:start size:94% position:6%
So we literally soundchecked
at 30 Rock

00:05:58.257 --> 00:06:00.193 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then took a helicopter
to the gig,

00:06:00.193 --> 00:06:04.564 align:start size:94% position:6%
played for 2 and a half hours,
took a helicopter back,

00:06:04.564 --> 00:06:06.766 align:start size:94% position:6%
were Mick Jagger's backing ban
on the show,

00:06:06.766 --> 00:06:08.568 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then we played
the after-party.

00:06:08.568 --> 00:06:09.836 line:92%
Do you remember the after-party?

00:06:09.836 --> 00:06:11.204 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That was
a fantastic after-party.

00:06:11.204 --> 00:06:13.773
-It was the greatest day
of my life! It was amazing

00:06:13.773 --> 00:06:16.476 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's crazy
that you were on the toile

00:06:16.476 --> 00:06:17.443 size:81% position:41% line:92%
when you got that call

00:06:17.443 --> 00:06:19.679 align:start size:94% position:6%
because I remember
being on the other side.

00:06:19.679 --> 00:06:21.914 align:start size:94% position:6%
Lorne called you
from the toilet, as well.

00:06:21.914 --> 00:06:24.417
-Interesting. Well, that's
how these deals are made.

00:06:24.417 --> 00:06:26.853 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, I remember
he came out of his bathroo

00:06:26.853 --> 00:06:28.921 align:start size:94% position:6%
and said,
"Foo Fighters are in."

00:06:28.921 --> 00:06:29.822 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:06:29.822 --> 00:06:32.658
-I don't know if you know.
We were actually FaceTiming.

00:06:32.658 --> 00:06:33.760 size:78% position:39% line:92%
I don't -- Did you --

00:06:33.760 --> 00:06:36.696 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh. So you knew. You knew
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:06:36.696 --> 00:06:38.598 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Do you remember
who was the host

00:06:38.598 --> 00:06:40.833 align:start size:94% position:6%
the first time Nirvana
was on the show?

00:06:40.833 --> 00:06:44.670
-First time Nirvana was on the
show, the host was Rob Morrow.

00:06:44.670 --> 00:06:46.072 line:92%
-Wow. And then the second time

00:06:46.072 --> 00:06:48.307 align:start size:94% position:6%
-...who was from that show
"Northern Exposure."

00:06:48.307 --> 00:06:50.476 size:81% position:41%
-You guys were on with
Barkley once, right?

00:06:50.476 --> 00:06:52.678 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, Charles Barkley!
That's right!

00:06:52.678 --> 00:06:54.781 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And I remember --

00:06:54.781 --> 00:06:56.416 align:start size:94% position:6%
Our bass player,
Krist Novoselic.

00:06:56.416 --> 00:06:58.584 align:start size:94% position:6%
Krist Novoselic is 6'8."
Okay?

00:06:58.584 --> 00:07:00.787 align:start size:94% position:6%
The bass player for Nirvan
is very tall.

00:07:00.787 --> 00:07:06.692
And I remember when we wer
doing the promos that, you know,

00:07:06.692 --> 00:07:08.294 line:92%
on the Thursday before the show,

00:07:08.294 --> 00:07:12.765 align:start size:94% position:6%
I remember seeing Krist
tower over Charles Barkley

00:07:12.765 --> 00:07:15.468
and thinking, like, "Okay.
Now this is getting weird.

00:07:15.468 --> 00:07:16.936 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, now,
this is officially weird."

00:07:16.936 --> 00:07:19.772 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right. Well, it also
gives you a real appreciatio

00:07:19.772 --> 00:07:22.975 align:start size:94% position:6%
for how hard Barkley worke
for those rebounds

00:07:22.975 --> 00:07:26.145
when he's not even taller
than the tallest guy in Nirvana.

00:07:26.145 --> 00:07:27.947 align:start size:94% position:6%
There was a long gap
between Barkley hosting.

00:07:27.947 --> 00:07:29.248 align:start size:94% position:6%
He's done it quite
a few times recently.

00:07:29.248 --> 00:07:33.352
But I remember him regaling us
with stories of the first time

00:07:33.352 --> 00:07:35.521
