and you realized

00:07:58.644 --> 00:08:02.248
that was a great opportunity
because, being fans of the show,

00:08:02.248 --> 00:08:04.784 align:start size:94% position:6%
you knew that meant
that he would introduce you,

00:08:04.784 --> 00:08:06.118 line:92%
this being the Foo Fighters.

00:08:06.118 --> 00:08:07.920 size:88% position:44%
-Yeah, you know, I mean,
everybody has their own

00:08:07.920 --> 00:08:10.389 align:start size:94% position:6%
Christopher Walken
impersonation, and, of course,

00:08:10.389 --> 00:08:14.160
we were huge fans
from everything, from, you know,

00:08:14.160 --> 00:08:16.229 align:start size:94% position:6%
"The Deer Hunter"
to "Pulp Fiction."

00:08:16.229 --> 00:08:17.830 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, we just kind of
loved the guy.

00:08:17.830 --> 00:08:22.969 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he came up to us befor
introducing us, and he said --

00:08:22.969 --> 00:08:23.669 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
He said...

00:08:23.669 --> 00:08:27.440 align:start size:94% position:6%
[As Walken] "The accent.
Is it on 'Foo' or 'Fighters'?"

00:08:27.440 --> 00:08:32.612
And I knew if I said "Fighters,"
I knew what would happen.

00:08:32.612 --> 00:08:34.614 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, so,
the house lights went down

00:08:34.614 --> 00:08:38.384 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the camera hit him,
and he said...

00:08:38.384 --> 00:08:41.120
[As Walken] "Ladies and
gentlemen, Foo FIGHTERS!"

00:08:41.120 --> 00:08:43.656 line:92%
And so that's how we referred --

00:08:43.656 --> 00:08:45.992 align:start size:94% position:6%
We refer to ourselves
as Foo FIGHTERS,

00:08:45.992 --> 00:08:48.761 line:92%
you know, still to this day.

00:08:48.761 --> 00:08:49.862 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-Very, very impressive

00:08:49.862 --> 00:08:54.066 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you saw that opportunit
and took it.

00:08:54.066 --> 00:08:55.801 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Always thinking.
Always thinking.

00:08:55.801 --> 00:08:58.671 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Hey, thanks so much.
So excited you're doing music.

00:08:58.671 --> 00:08:59.639 line:92%
And you also -- Real quick -

00:08:59.639 --> 00:09:01.807 align:start size:94% position:6%
You have a documentary
that you directed.

00:09:01.807 --> 00:09:04.644
Another thing that most
musicians have in common.

00:09:04.644 --> 00:09:07.480 align:start size:94% position:6%
Not just parents who support
their music early on,

00:09:07.480 --> 00:09:08.381 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
but life in a van.

00:09:08.381 --> 00:09:10.850
And I'm certainly looking
forward to seeing that.

00:09:10.850 --> 00:09:13.753
Because -- Do you miss -- Do you
miss your days in the band

00:09:13.753 --> 00:09:16.656 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because I can think
it's probably a little bit

00:09:16.656 --> 00:09:17.423 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
like your youth?

00:09:17.423 --> 00:09:19.825
Like, you miss it but also
don't want to do it again.

00:09:19.825 --> 00:09:22.862
-Well, you know, the great thing
about having that experience

00:09:22.862 --> 00:09:26.065 align:start size:94% position:6%
is that you sort of
rely on that for --

00:09:26.065 --> 00:09:27.733 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, to keep
everything in perspective

00:09:27.733 --> 00:09:30.036 align:start size:94% position:6%
for all the rewards and things
that come after.

00:09:30.036 --> 00:09:32.405
But the cool thing about tha
documentary is that, you know,

00:09:32.405 --> 00:09:35.408
I interviewed Ringo and Duff
and Slash from Guns N' Roses

00:09:35.408 --> 00:09:38.144 align:start size:94% position:6%
and Steven Tyler
and Brian Johnson from AC/DC

00:09:38.144 --> 00:09:40.246 line:92%
all of these huge rock stars

00:09:40.246 --> 00:09:42.381 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I also interviewed
some young bands,

00:09:42.381 --> 00:09:45.017 align:start size:94% position:6%
a band called Starcrawler,
a band called Radkey.

00:09:45.017 --> 00:09:47.119 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, you know,
what I realized is that, like,

00:09:47.119 --> 00:09:52.091 align:start size:94% position:6%
the kids in Radkey
are having the same experience

00:09:52.091 --> 00:09:55.494 align:start size:94% position:6%
that the Beatles had
when they were their age.

00:09:55.494 --> 00:09:56.596 line:92%
It's a 60-year difference,

00:09:56.596 --> 00:09:59.899 align:start size:94% position:6%
but it all comes down
to that thing

00:09:59.899 --> 00:10:01.500 align:start size:94% position:6%
that makes you
throw your life away

00:10:01.500 --> 00:10:04.604 align:start size:94% position:6%
and just jump in a stinky va
with your friends.

00:10:04.604 --> 00:10:08.207 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, yeah. I mean, do I miss it
Sometimes.

00:10:08.207 --> 00:10:12.945
Do I -- Do I prefer, you know,
a nice G5 every once in a while?

00:10:12.945 --> 00:10:14.547 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Of course!

00:10:14.547 --> 00:10:17.183 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Treat yourself.
Hey, thank you so much.

00:10:17.183 --> 00:10:19.385 size:78% position:39%
It's always a delight
to talk to you, Dave.

00:10:19.385 --> 00:10:21.654 align:start size:94% position:6%
"From Cradle to Stage"
is available on Paramount+

00:10:21.654 --> 00:10:23.823 size:81% position:41%
And "What Drives Us"
is currently streaming

00:10:23.823 --> 00:10:24.924 line:92%
on The Coda Collection channel

00:10:24.924 --> 00:10:27.994 align:start size:94% position:6%
exclusively on
Amazon Prime Video.

